# Tailwind CSS & Radix UI — production design contract

SaaSForge Elite’s **core UI is native Tailwind + inline SVGs**
(`components/ui/button.tsx`, `lib/ui/layout-classes.ts`). Do not add shadcn
or a second icon pack to the kit itself unless the product owner asks.

When a **client project** (Enterprise license) adds Radix, follow this
contract so a11y and theming stay coherent.

## Tailwind (this kit and client apps)

- Tailwind **v4** (`@import "tailwindcss"`, `@theme` in `app/globals.css`).
  No `tailwind.config.ts` required for the core kit.
- Semantic class maps live in `lib/ui/layout-classes.ts`. Do not paste
  8-class strings into five screens — extract a variant helper
  (`navLinkClassName`, `chatBubbleClassName`).
- Join classes with `cn()` in `lib/ui/cn.ts`. Do not add `clsx` /
  `tailwind-merge` unless conflict resolution is actually needed.
- Dark mode: `html.dark` toggled by `useThemePreference` + inline boot
  script. Use `dark:` variants, not a second stylesheet.
- No inline `style={{}}` except runtime values (tilt transform, CSS
  variables). Prefer tokens: `--color-accent`, `glass-panel`.
- Focus: visible rings on every interactive control. Do not
  `outline-none` without a replacement.

## Forms and content

- Every input has a `<label htmlFor>` (see `components/ui/text-field.tsx`).
- Errors use `role="alert"`. Pending buttons disable and announce state.
- Self-closing JSX: `<input />`, `<img />`, `<hr />`.

## Radix (client projects only)

If you add `@radix-ui/react-*`:

- Own **behavior** (focus trap, dismiss, arrow keys, `aria-*`). Own
  **look** with Tailwind. Do not import Radix themes or a copy-paste
  shadcn `components/ui` dump into this kit’s `components/ui`.
- Prefer these primitives when the native element is insufficient:
  Dialog, DropdownMenu, Popover, Tooltip, Tabs, Checkbox, Switch.
- Controlled state stays in a hook (`useComposerDraft` pattern). The
  Radix root only receives `open` / `onOpenChange`.
- Portals must render inside the app shell so theme class `dark`
  still applies.
- `modal={true}` dialogs must lock body scroll (see
  `useMobileNavigation`) and restore it on unmount.
- Do not nest two modal focus traps.
- Keep bundle cost honest: import the primitive, not `@radix-ui/react`.

## Motion and marketing

- Landing motion is CSS (`animate-rise`, `animate-aurora`). Do not add
  Framer Motion for a fade-in.
- The product look is Linear-like SaaS, **not** a video-editor /
  film-portfolio aesthetic.
